⚠️  THIS LICENCE IS A PLACEHOLDER.

    It has not been reviewed by a lawyer, and the commercial terms below are a
    starting point for that conversation rather than a decision. Do not publish
    this package to npm until the licence has been settled — a licence is very
    hard to tighten after the fact, because every existing user keeps the terms
    they downloaded under.

    The choice to make is roughly:

      (a) MIT / Apache-2.0 — maximum adoption, no licence revenue, and the SDK
          becomes a distribution channel for the hosted product rather than a
          product itself.
      (b) Source-available with a paid commercial tier (the shape drafted
          below) — revenue per commercial user, slower adoption, and an
          enforcement burden you have to be willing to carry.
      (c) Dual licence — free for open-source projects, paid for closed ones.

    (b) is drafted here only because it matches the revenue reasoning that put
    the SDK on the roadmap. It is not a recommendation.

